    <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 14px 0;">Payment address data is a microcosm of this broader problem. Institutions rushing to deploy AI-driven payment automation on top of unstructured address data are building on sand. The primary culprit? Ambiguous, free-text address data that no automation engine can reliably parse.</p>

    <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 20px 0;">Format compliance gives you the syntax. Data readiness gives you the semantics. <strong style="font-weight:700;">AI models need the semantics.</strong> Yet across the payments industry, the conversation remains fixated on message format. Nobody is asking whether the data inside those messages is AI-ready.</p>

